mid-voice downloads third-party model weights at runtime. Those carry their own
terms, and two of the defaults are more restrictive than MIT:

  Whisper (large-v3)          MIT
  NLLB-200 (distilled-1.3B)   CC-BY-NC 4.0                     non-commercial
  XTTS-v2                     Coqui Public Model License       non-commercial

Running the default configuration therefore does not clear you for commercial
use. See docs/MODELS.md for the licence of every model and for the option
combination that keeps the whole stack permissive.
